      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "With the advent and popularity of Internet-based distribution of files
    in compressed audio formats such as MP3s, sales of CDs began to decline in the
    2000s. \r\n-->For example, between 2000 and 2008, despite overall growth in music
    sales and one anomalous year of increase, major-label CD sales declined overall
    by 20%. \r\n-->Despite rapidly declining sales year-over-year, the pervasiveness
    of the technology lingered for a time, with companies placing CDs in pharmacies,
    supermarkets, and filling station convenience stores to target buyers less likely
    to be able to use Internet-based distribution. "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
